[[:db/retract 17592186123050 :answer-field/choices 17592186123051] [:db/retract 17592186123050 :answer-field/choices 17592186123052] [:db/retract 17592186123050 :answer-field/choices 17592186123053] [:db/retract 17592186123050 :answer-field/choices 17592186123054] [:db/retract 17592186123050 :answer-field/choices 17592186123055] [:db/retract 17592186122474 :answer-field/choices 17592186122475] [:db/retract 17592186122474 :answer-field/choices 17592186122476] [:db/retract 17592186122474 :answer-field/choices 17592186122477] [:db/retract 17592186122474 :answer-field/choices 17592186122478] [:db/retract 17592186122474 :answer-field/choices 17592186122479] {:db/id 17592186124454 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-1c716d26-2571-5872-95a3-6c53428692e0" "question-7d7bf3ca-d3c4-5a27-836b-a5e78d17fbc9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124455 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-43788191-a65e-5058-bbfd-37ff934a1aa8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124456 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-caca4712-f17f-5ed4-8f57-6c6c5c27d1ce" "question-2ac861e6-ea7e-53f0-b9c2-bba93cd70561"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186125075 :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2})-3{y}^{3}$, find the equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point where $(x,y)=(\\sqrt{\\pi },2).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent line to the level curve $f(x,y)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(x,y)=(\\sqrt{\\pi },2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2})-3{y}^{3})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2})-3{y}^{3})\\,j \\\\  & =-2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2})\\,i-9{y}^{2}\\,j \\\\ ∇\\,f(\\sqrt{\\pi },2) & =-2\\sqrt{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡((\\sqrt{\\pi })^{2})i-9(2)^{2}\\,j \\\\  & =-2\\sqrt{\\pi }\\cdot 0\\,i-36\\,j \\\\  & =-36\\,j \\\\  & =⟨0,-36⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(\\sqrt{\\pi },2)\\cdot ⟨x-\\sqrt{\\pi },\\,y-2⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨0,-36⟩\\cdot ⟨x-\\sqrt{\\pi },\\,y-2⟩ & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186123050 :answer-field/correct "answer-2b0197ad-d5e0-50ec-8157-0c06f4986576" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2b0197ad-d5e0-50ec-8157-0c06f4986576" "answer-e5bdc0c7-03d3-58fa-b3e6-6a56b32f6d75" "answer-341d1b1c-4578-5521-9b08-b2e4e4af8a34" "answer-351713ea-d6ad-5a99-b2a8-0ed43fff911d" "answer-f85e4345-3a7c-5b21-b5a8-d864dc102736"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2b0197ad-d5e0-50ec-8157-0c06f4986576" :answer/id #uuid "2b0197ad-d5e0-50ec-8157-0c06f4986576" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,-36⟩\\cdot ⟨x-\\sqrt{\\pi },\\,y-2⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e5bdc0c7-03d3-58fa-b3e6-6a56b32f6d75" :answer/id #uuid "e5bdc0c7-03d3-58fa-b3e6-6a56b32f6d75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,12⟩\\cdot ⟨x-\\sqrt{\\pi },\\,y-2⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-341d1b1c-4578-5521-9b08-b2e4e4af8a34" :answer/id #uuid "341d1b1c-4578-5521-9b08-b2e4e4af8a34" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-\\sqrt{\\pi },\\,y-2⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-351713ea-d6ad-5a99-b2a8-0ed43fff911d" :answer/id #uuid "351713ea-d6ad-5a99-b2a8-0ed43fff911d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨36,0⟩\\cdot ⟨x-\\sqrt{\\pi },\\,y-2⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f85e4345-3a7c-5b21-b5a8-d864dc102736" :answer/id #uuid "f85e4345-3a7c-5b21-b5a8-d864dc102736" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨6,9⟩\\cdot ⟨x-\\sqrt{\\pi },\\,y-2⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124979 :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y)=3{x}^{2}+2x{y}^{2}-y$, find the equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point where $(x,y)=(-1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent line to the level curve $f(x,y)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(x,y)=(-1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{x}^{2}+2x{y}^{2}-y)\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{x}^{2}+2x{y}^{2}-y)\\,j \\\\  & =(6x+2{y}^{2})\\text{ }i+(4xy-1)\\text{ }j \\\\ ∇\\,f(-1,1) & =(6(-1)+2(1)^{2})\\,i+(4(-1)(1)-1)\\,j \\\\  & =-4\\,i-5\\,j \\\\  & =⟨-4,-5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(-1,1)\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨-4,-5⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y-1⟩ & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186122474 :answer-field/correct "answer-aad3ab95-80b7-58a9-8f7a-b59b2f76d6e1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-aad3ab95-80b7-58a9-8f7a-b59b2f76d6e1" "answer-81b0821b-7e46-5c33-9092-7826606b26db" "answer-b3e86513-1b68-561a-a8d3-dbdeb9989260" "answer-dad53699-365d-5be5-97a0-c5dd9eb33c08" "answer-3567d85d-c8e4-5c8e-a5fa-9a03f4e73154"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aad3ab95-80b7-58a9-8f7a-b59b2f76d6e1" :answer/id #uuid "aad3ab95-80b7-58a9-8f7a-b59b2f76d6e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-4,-5⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y-1⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-81b0821b-7e46-5c33-9092-7826606b26db" :answer/id #uuid "81b0821b-7e46-5c33-9092-7826606b26db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨2,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y-1⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b3e86513-1b68-561a-a8d3-dbdeb9989260" :answer/id #uuid "b3e86513-1b68-561a-a8d3-dbdeb9989260" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨5,3⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y-1⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dad53699-365d-5be5-97a0-c5dd9eb33c08" :answer/id #uuid "dad53699-365d-5be5-97a0-c5dd9eb33c08" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨5,4⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y-1⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3567d85d-c8e4-5c8e-a5fa-9a03f4e73154" :answer/id #uuid "3567d85d-c8e4-5c8e-a5fa-9a03f4e73154" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨6,2⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y-1⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1c716d26-2571-5872-95a3-6c53428692e0" :question/id #uuid "1c716d26-2571-5872-95a3-6c53428692e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-130102" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}-y)$ find the equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point where $(x,y)=(0,\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent line to the level curve $f(x,y)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(x,y)=(0,\\pi ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}-y))\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}-y))\\,j \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2}-y)\\,i-\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2}-y)\\,j \\\\ ∇f(0,\\pi ) & =2(0)\\operatorname{cos}⁡({0}^{2}-\\pi )\\,i-\\operatorname{cos}⁡({0}^{2}-\\pi )\\,j \\\\  & =0\\,i+j \\\\  & =⟨0,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(0,\\pi )\\cdot ⟨x-0,\\,y-\\pi ⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨0,1⟩\\cdot ⟨x,\\,y-\\pi ⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4d61b3aa-4d6d-50f6-8ee7-8efa72e96369"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4d61b3aa-4d6d-50f6-8ee7-8efa72e96369" :answer-field/id #uuid "4d61b3aa-4d6d-50f6-8ee7-8efa72e96369" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-bd84b736-12f3-529d-aed6-fa8d36f93fd5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8cda681d-6db9-54b3-bd78-3fc12602c207" "answer-c943eb76-7894-538d-b2d8-85356d2d0217" "answer-caf722cf-879e-502b-9dcd-ed9b635a2c2c" "answer-bd84b736-12f3-529d-aed6-fa8d36f93fd5" "answer-7cd3b229-87d5-5fe0-bf43-96e6859b0b2a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8cda681d-6db9-54b3-bd78-3fc12602c207" :answer/id #uuid "8cda681d-6db9-54b3-bd78-3fc12602c207" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-1,0⟩\\cdot ⟨x,\\,y-\\pi ⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c943eb76-7894-538d-b2d8-85356d2d0217" :answer/id #uuid "c943eb76-7894-538d-b2d8-85356d2d0217" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-1,1⟩\\cdot ⟨x,\\,y-\\pi ⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-caf722cf-879e-502b-9dcd-ed9b635a2c2c" :answer/id #uuid "caf722cf-879e-502b-9dcd-ed9b635a2c2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-2,1⟩\\cdot ⟨x,\\,y-\\pi ⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bd84b736-12f3-529d-aed6-fa8d36f93fd5" :answer/id #uuid "bd84b736-12f3-529d-aed6-fa8d36f93fd5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,1⟩\\cdot ⟨x,\\,y-\\pi ⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7cd3b229-87d5-5fe0-bf43-96e6859b0b2a" :answer/id #uuid "7cd3b229-87d5-5fe0-bf43-96e6859b0b2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,2⟩\\cdot ⟨x,\\,y-\\pi ⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-7d7bf3ca-d3c4-5a27-836b-a5e78d17fbc9" :question/id #uuid "7d7bf3ca-d3c4-5a27-836b-a5e78d17fbc9" :question/math-academy-id "q-36397" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y)=3xy+4x+6y-5{y}^{2}$, find the equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point where $(x,y)=(1,2).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent line to the level curve $f(x,y)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(x,y)=(1,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3xy+4x+6y-5{y}^{2})i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3xy+4x+6y-5{y}^{2})j \\\\  & =(3y+4)\\,i+(3x+6-10y)\\,j \\\\ ∇\\,f(1,2) & =(3(2)+4)\\,i+(3(1)+6-10(2))\\,j \\\\  & =10\\,i-11\\,j \\\\  & =⟨10,-11⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(1,2)\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-2⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨10,-11⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-2⟩ & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6a5737f4-7f36-5112-b8c8-5f6aec3f9ccd"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6a5737f4-7f36-5112-b8c8-5f6aec3f9ccd" :answer-field/id #uuid "6a5737f4-7f36-5112-b8c8-5f6aec3f9ccd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e6bd368a-c465-55d9-8a07-4d1ad01503a5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e6bd368a-c465-55d9-8a07-4d1ad01503a5" "answer-16af8390-5001-553a-b0f4-0d97c561270f" "answer-2a9a977b-a2a7-597d-813d-3e1b77c5b121" "answer-bc35064f-3e58-53ec-9341-b4fdb731d8dd" "answer-e5a87d66-7787-5592-a30b-ee6c5d027bd7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e6bd368a-c465-55d9-8a07-4d1ad01503a5" :answer/id #uuid "e6bd368a-c465-55d9-8a07-4d1ad01503a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨10,-11⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-2⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-16af8390-5001-553a-b0f4-0d97c561270f" :answer/id #uuid "16af8390-5001-553a-b0f4-0d97c561270f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨11,-10⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-2⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2a9a977b-a2a7-597d-813d-3e1b77c5b121" :answer/id #uuid "2a9a977b-a2a7-597d-813d-3e1b77c5b121" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨12,14⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-2⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bc35064f-3e58-53ec-9341-b4fdb731d8dd" :answer/id #uuid "bc35064f-3e58-53ec-9341-b4fdb731d8dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨5,-6⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-2⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e5a87d66-7787-5592-a30b-ee6c5d027bd7" :answer/id #uuid "e5a87d66-7787-5592-a30b-ee6c5d027bd7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨6,5⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-2⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-43788191-a65e-5058-bbfd-37ff934a1aa8" :question/id #uuid "43788191-a65e-5058-bbfd-37ff934a1aa8" :question/math-academy-id "q-72403" :question/problem "Consider the plane curve $(x-y)^{2}=2x-y.$ Find a tangent vector to that curve at the point $(2,0).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-y)^{2} & =2x-y \\\\ (x-y)^{2}-2x+y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y)=(x-y)^{2}-2x+y$, our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=0.$ \n\nA tangent vector to the level curve that passes through the point $(2,0)$ can be computed as follows:\n\n$$\nt(2,0)={f}_{y}(2,0)i-{f}_{x}(2,0)j\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $t(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(2,0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}((x-y)^{2}-2x+y)i-\\frac{∂}{∂x}((x-y)^{2}-2x+y)j \\\\  & =(-2(x-y)+1)i-(2(x-y)-2)j \\\\ t(2,0) & =(-2((2)-(0))+1)\\,i-((2((2)-(0))-2)\\,j \\\\  & =-3\\,i-2\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our tangent vector is $-3\\,i-2\\,j.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-74d8ed8e-549b-58fd-a410-9d0b085953e8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-74d8ed8e-549b-58fd-a410-9d0b085953e8" :answer-field/id #uuid "74d8ed8e-549b-58fd-a410-9d0b085953e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c60ad1d3-95a7-5a9f-b2b9-64da4df122a3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f8735719-d369-5e0e-a1c4-c3a71df5f0ee" "answer-c60ad1d3-95a7-5a9f-b2b9-64da4df122a3" "answer-f692be5a-8425-517e-a612-23b54fc9103d" "answer-9548efa7-b337-5098-83fd-68445ff80070" "answer-e6e79c61-6c42-5702-a833-be284f78ce16"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f8735719-d369-5e0e-a1c4-c3a71df5f0ee" :answer/id #uuid "f8735719-d369-5e0e-a1c4-c3a71df5f0ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\,i-5\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c60ad1d3-95a7-5a9f-b2b9-64da4df122a3" :answer/id #uuid "c60ad1d3-95a7-5a9f-b2b9-64da4df122a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3\\,i-2\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f692be5a-8425-517e-a612-23b54fc9103d" :answer/id #uuid "f692be5a-8425-517e-a612-23b54fc9103d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5\\,i-4\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9548efa7-b337-5098-83fd-68445ff80070" :answer/id #uuid "9548efa7-b337-5098-83fd-68445ff80070" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,i-3\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e6e79c61-6c42-5702-a833-be284f78ce16" :answer/id #uuid "e6e79c61-6c42-5702-a833-be284f78ce16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\,i+5\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-caca4712-f17f-5ed4-8f57-6c6c5c27d1ce" :question/id #uuid "caca4712-f17f-5ed4-8f57-6c6c5c27d1ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-130213" :question/problem "At which point on the curve $x{y}^{2}=3-2y$ is the tangent vector to the curve perpendicular to the vector $i?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x{y}^{2} & =3-2y \\\\ x{y}^{2}+2y & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y)=x{y}^{2}+2y,$ our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=3.$ \n\nA tangent vector to the level curve can be computed as follows:\n\n$$\nt(x,y)={f}_{y}(x,y)\\,i-{f}_{x}(x,y)\\,j\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $t(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t(x,y) & ={f}_{y}(x,y)\\,i-{f}_{x}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{y}^{2}+2y)\\,i-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x{y}^{2}+2y)\\,j \\\\  & =(2xy+2)\\,i-{y}^{2}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince our tangent vector needs to be perpendicular to $i,$ we must have $t\\cdot i=0.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)\\cdot i & =0 \\\\ ((2xy+2)\\,i-{y}^{2}\\,j)\\cdot i & =0 \\\\ 2xy+2 & =0 \\\\ xy+1 & =0 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $y=-\\frac{1}{x}$ into the equation of our curve gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x{y}^{2} & =3-2y \\\\ x{(-\\frac{1}{x})}^{2} & =3-2(-\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\ \\frac{1}{x} & =3+\\frac{2}{x} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x} & =-3 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, for $x=-\\frac{1}{3},$ we get $y=3,$ and the corresponding point is $(-\\frac{1}{3},3).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-16678482-e75d-56bd-a681-d31f80ad72e2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-16678482-e75d-56bd-a681-d31f80ad72e2" :answer-field/id #uuid "16678482-e75d-56bd-a681-d31f80ad72e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cc49cf9f-93a9-5729-904e-6ab3eebbf63c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cc49cf9f-93a9-5729-904e-6ab3eebbf63c" "answer-fa96e6a2-688c-5137-81fa-3a6eabc7070a" "answer-be9a2db1-529d-5628-9061-7052c51aa8d2" "answer-f66bf744-8b15-5c45-869d-f7226d3e3a1a" "answer-cf37dabf-a5f5-5488-94e7-124530583cd7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cc49cf9f-93a9-5729-904e-6ab3eebbf63c" :answer/id #uuid "cc49cf9f-93a9-5729-904e-6ab3eebbf63c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\frac{1}{3},3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fa96e6a2-688c-5137-81fa-3a6eabc7070a" :answer/id #uuid "fa96e6a2-688c-5137-81fa-3a6eabc7070a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\frac{1}{4},2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-be9a2db1-529d-5628-9061-7052c51aa8d2" :answer/id #uuid "be9a2db1-529d-5628-9061-7052c51aa8d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,\\frac{3}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f66bf744-8b15-5c45-869d-f7226d3e3a1a" :answer/id #uuid "f66bf744-8b15-5c45-869d-f7226d3e3a1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1,1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cf37dabf-a5f5-5488-94e7-124530583cd7" :answer/id #uuid "cf37dabf-a5f5-5488-94e7-124530583cd7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(5,-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2ac861e6-ea7e-53f0-b9c2-bba93cd70561" :question/id #uuid "2ac861e6-ea7e-53f0-b9c2-bba93cd70561" :question/math-academy-id "q-130227" :question/problem "At which point on the curve ${x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=xy$ is the tangent vector to the curve perpendicular to the vector $i?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-{y}^{2} & =xy \\\\ {x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-xy & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y)={x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-xy,$ our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=0.$ \n\nA tangent vector to the level curve can be computed as follows:\n\n$$\nt(x,y)={f}_{y}(x,y)\\,i-{f}_{x}(x,y)\\,j\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $t(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t(x,y) & ={f}_{y}(x,y)\\,i-{f}_{x}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-xy)\\,i-\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-xy)\\,j \\\\  & =(-2y-x)\\,i-(2x-y)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince our tangent vector needs to be perpendicular to $i,$ we must have $t\\cdot i=0.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)\\cdot i & =0 \\\\ ((-2y-x)\\,i-(2x-y)\\,j)\\cdot i & =0 \\\\ -2y-x & =0 \\\\ x & =-2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-2y$ into the equation of our curve gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-{y}^{2} & =xy \\\\ (-2y)^{2}-{y}^{2} & =(-2y)y \\\\ 4{y}^{2}-{y}^{2} & =-2{y}^{2} \\\\ 5{y}^{2} & =0 \\\\ y & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, for $y=0,$ we get $x=0,$ and the corresponding point is $(0,0).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4746e6c2-e2ff-5920-bf56-69cc85ac1d10"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4746e6c2-e2ff-5920-bf56-69cc85ac1d10" :answer-field/id #uuid "4746e6c2-e2ff-5920-bf56-69cc85ac1d10" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-64cdcf40-7d0f-5cd1-9631-68535525b11a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-64cdcf40-7d0f-5cd1-9631-68535525b11a" "answer-269f786d-89ec-5cd5-a946-ff7a25f5bfdc" "answer-c6b197ac-be86-5a79-bafe-30616fa5194f" "answer-f223ad97-8210-5437-a5b5-584c17f1bb93" "answer-9652c686-4a06-5958-9b68-3ac0c59d9c39"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-64cdcf40-7d0f-5cd1-9631-68535525b11a" :answer/id #uuid "64cdcf40-7d0f-5cd1-9631-68535525b11a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-269f786d-89ec-5cd5-a946-ff7a25f5bfdc" :answer/id #uuid "269f786d-89ec-5cd5-a946-ff7a25f5bfdc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2,1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c6b197ac-be86-5a79-bafe-30616fa5194f" :answer/id #uuid "c6b197ac-be86-5a79-bafe-30616fa5194f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{5+\\sqrt{5}}{2},\\sqrt{5})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f223ad97-8210-5437-a5b5-584c17f1bb93" :answer/id #uuid "f223ad97-8210-5437-a5b5-584c17f1bb93" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}+1}{2},1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9652c686-4a06-5958-9b68-3ac0c59d9c39" :answer/id #uuid "9652c686-4a06-5958-9b68-3ac0c59d9c39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\s